    "The capture spans several programs (Associate of Arts in Business intro, Business Information Systems requirements without its program heading, Business Leadership, and a partial Child Development entry); this ledger covers Bachelor of Arts in Business Leadership, the only program whose title and full requirements are both in the capture. Confirm this is the intended program.",
    "The capture does not explicitly state the credit unit (semester vs. quarter); 'semester' is assumed from the generic 'credits' wording and should be verified.",
    "Global Campus Foundations courses are taken from the standard institution-wide sequence, which states 'Courses may be substituted'; the capture does not list the allowed substitutions or which category each course fulfills (e.g., Quantitative Reasoning, Natural Scientist Perspective).",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled as the first course and counts toward 3 elective credits; students with fewer than 30 transferable credits also take GEN 104 for 3 elective credits. These are inside the 42-credit elective block and are not listed separately.",
    "Residency requirement: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University as a matriculated student; the capture does not tie this to specific courses.",
    "A minimum of 30 upper-division credits is required, including 18 upper-division credits in the major; the capture does not define which course numbers count as upper-division.",
    "MGT 460 must be taken last in the program; the capture does not state whether it must be completed at UAGC.",
    "Prerequisites noted in the capture (e.g., BUS 318 and BUS 370 accept BUS 201 as an alternative) reference courses not otherwise listed in this program's requirements.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 is required for all coursework attempted at the University."
